## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)

### 1. Can I edit a PDF without installing software?

Yes. You can use a browser-based PDF editor to make many common changes without installing dedicated PDF software.

### 2. Can I edit a PDF on my phone?

Yes. Many modern online PDF editors work through mobile web browsers, allowing you to edit PDFs from smartphones and tablets.

### 3. Can I add text to a PDF without software?

Yes. If the PDF editor supports text insertion, you can add new text directly to the PDF using your browser.

### 4. Can I add a signature to a PDF online?

Many PDF editors provide signature or drawing tools that allow you to add a signature to a document.

### 5. Can I edit a scanned PDF?

A scanned PDF may require OCR to recognize its text before the text can be edited like normal PDF text. The availability of OCR depends on the PDF editor.

### 6. Is an online PDF editor free?

Some online PDF editors offer free PDF editing features. The available features and limits vary between different services.

### 7. Do I need an account to edit a PDF online?

Not necessarily. Some browser-based PDF editors allow users to edit documents without creating an account. Check the requirements of the particular tool you choose.

